cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use MiraProt in your research, please cite the MiraProt software
  release used for your analysis and the associated publication when available.

title: "MiraProt"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Schmalen"
    given-names: "Adrian"

abstract: >-
  MiraProt is a modular R Shiny-based platform for integrated downstream
  proteomics analysis of processed protein-level abundance data. It connects
  data preparation, differential expression analysis, dimensionality
  reduction, functional enrichment, gene set enrichment analysis, protein
  interaction network analysis, protein set comparison, and visualization
  within a single interactive workflow.

repository-code: "https://github.com/AdSchmalen/MiraProt"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - proteomics
  - bioinformatics
  - R
  - Shiny
  - downstream proteomics analysis
  - differential expression
  - dimensionality reduction
  - principal component analysis
  - gene set enrichment analysis
  - functional enrichment
  - protein interaction networks
  - data visualization
  - research software

